## Structure

```
├── manage.py                                <- Django management
├── config/
│   ├── settings.py                           <- Django settings
│   ├── urls.py                               <- URL routing
│   ├── wsgi.py / asgi.py                    <- WSGI/ASGI entry points
├── core/
│   └── app_error.py                          <- error classes
├── domain/<module>/
│   ├── entity.py                             <- domain entity (pure Python)
│   ├── repository.py                         <- repository interface (ABC)
│   └── service.py                            <- domain service
├── application/<module>/
│   ├── use_case.py                           <- use cases
│   └── dto.py                                <- DTOs
└── infrastructure/
    ├── persistence/<module>_repository.py    <- Django ORM adapter
    └── web/<module>_router.py               <- DRF views & urls
```

Call direction: `infrastructure -> application -> domain`. Domain never imports
from infrastructure or application.

